{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014foZTPHC5ECTHAYWZau7DX","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Architectural spec for the `build-tests-fix-from-spec` host project.\n2\t#\n3\t# `build tests` reads it to resolve which suite owns a scenario: the\n4\t# tests/<service>/ tree whose `service:` matches the scenario's. Its word\n5\t# mapping says how each product word is built, and how a step\n6\t# definition observes it; the step definitions follow from it.\n7\t\n8\tarchitecture:\n9\t  testing:\n10\t    framework: go-test\n11\t    commands:\n12\t      record: go test -tags bdd -json -count=1 ./tests/mcp/...\n13\t      replay: go test -tags bdd -json -count=1 ./tests/mcp/...\n14\t      live: go test -tags bdd -json -count=1 ./tests/mcp/...\n15\t  services:\n16\t    - name: mcp-service\n17\t      path: services/mcp-service\n18\t      language: go\n19\t  terms:\n20\t    - term: MCP server\n21\t      technical: >-\n22\t        The mcp-service process, listening on 127.0.0.1 at the port the\n23\t        MCP_PORT environment variable names, 7411 when it is unset. It\n24\t        answers GET /healthz with 200 once it is ready.\n25\t      observed_by: >-\n26\t        Resolve the address from MCP_PORT, 7411 when it is unset, and poll\n27\t        GET /healthz there until it answers 200, for at most 5 seconds. A\n28\t        server that never answers fails the step, naming the address it\n29\t        polled.\n30\t    - term: session\n31\t      technical: >-\n32\t        Opened by a JSON-RPC 2.0 request whose method is initialize,\n33\t        POSTed to /mcp with Content-Type application/json. The server's\n34\t        reply to it is the session's opening.\n35\t      observed_by: >-\n36\t        POST {\"jsonrpc\":\"2.0\",\"id\":1,\"method\":\"initialize\"} to /mcp at the\n37\t        server's address and keep the reply's status code and headers for\n38\t        the steps after. A Then step that finds no reply fails instead of\n39\t        passing.\n40\t    - term: ticket\n41\t      technical: >-\n42\t        The X-Session-Ticket header of the reply to initialize: 32\n43\t        lowercase hexadecimal characters. A reply without it opened no\n44\t        session, whatever its status.\n45\t      observed_by: >-\n46\t        Read the X-Session-Ticket header of the last reply. It must be 32\n47\t        lowercase hexadecimal characters on a 200 reply; a missing or\n48\t        malformed ticket fails, naming the status and the header value\n49\t        the reply carried.\n50\t    - term: protocol version\n51\t      technical: >-\n52\t        The X-MCP-Protocol header of the reply to initialize, a date in\n53\t        YYYY-MM-DD form, such as 2025-06-18.\n54\t      observed_by: >-\n55\t        Read the X-MCP-Protocol header of the last reply. It must be a\n56\t        date in YYYY-MM-DD form; a missing or malformed value fails,\n57\t        naming what the reply carried.\n58\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d7bb89b6-a713-42fc-9e4f-b74ed7e7984b","uuid":"ab9de084-20ae-455d-90f8-bbd4d7ef67d9","timestamp":"2026-10-25T11:51:34.984Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"{{CWD}}/docs/architecture/architecture.yaml","content":"# Architectural spec for the `build-tests-fix-from-spec` host project.\n#\n# `build tests` reads it to resolve which suite owns a scenario: the\n# tests/<service>/ tree whose `service:` matches the scenario's. Its word\n# mapping says how each product word is built, and how a step\n# definition observes it; the step definitions follow from it.\n\narchitecture:\n  testing:\n    framework: go-test\n    commands:\n      record: go test -tags bdd -json -count=1 ./tests/mcp/...\n      replay: go test -tags bdd -json -count=1 ./tests/mcp/...\n      live: go test -tags bdd -json -count=1 ./tests/mcp/...\n  services:\n    - name: mcp-service\n      path: services/mcp-service\n      language: go\n  terms:\n    - term: MCP server\n      technical: >-\n        The mcp-service process, listening on 127.0.0.1 at the port the\n        MCP_PORT environment variable names, 7411 when it is unset. It\n        answers GET /healthz with 200 once it is ready.\n      observed_by: >-\n        Resolve the address from MCP_PORT, 7411 when it is unset, and poll\n        GET /healthz there until it answers 200, for at most 5 seconds. A\n        server that never answers fails the step, naming the address it\n        polled.\n    - term: session\n      technical: >-\n        Opened by a JSON-RPC 2.0 request whose method is initialize,\n        POSTed to /mcp with Content-Type application/json. The server's\n        reply to it is the session's opening.\n      observed_by: >-\n        POST {\"jsonrpc\":\"2.0\",\"id\":1,\"method\":\"initialize\"} to /mcp at the\n        server's address and keep the reply's status code and headers for\n        the steps after. A Then step that finds no reply fails instead of\n        passing.\n    - term: ticket\n      technical: >-\n        The X-Session-Ticket header of the reply to initialize: 32\n        lowercase hexadecimal characters. A reply without it opened no\n        session, whatever its status.\n      observed_by: >-\n        Read the X-Session-Ticket header of the last reply. It must be 32\n        lowercase hexadecimal characters on a 200 reply; a missing or\n        malformed ticket fails, naming the status and the header value\n        the reply carried.\n    - term: protocol version\n      technical: >-\n        The X-MCP-Protocol header of the reply to initialize, a date in\n        YYYY-MM-DD form, such as 2025-06-18.\n      observed_by: >-\n        Read the X-MCP-Protocol header of the last reply. It must be a\n        date in YYYY-MM-DD form; a missing or malformed value fails,\n        naming what the reply carried.\n","numLines":58,"startLine":1,"totalLines":58}}}
